      "71": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "READING MIDI\n\nThe Read Note On/Off and Read CC nodes are there to read incomming midi data and split up the contents to better keep track of what is comming in.\n\nMIDI In inputs midi data into your wire patch.\n\nRead Node On outputs the incomming pitch, velocity and channel when a note is on.\n\nRead Node Off outputs the incomming pitch, velocity and channel when a note is off.\n\nRead CC outputs the CC message, the controller that sends the CC message and the channel.\n\nConnect a Midi controller to use the example."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 310,
          "width": 668.940185546875,
          "x": -42.84625244140625,
          "y": 78.11839294433594
        },
